<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Send_Card_Expiry_Email</name>
        <label>Send card expiry reminder to donor</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>431</locationY>
        <actionName>emailSimple</actionName>
        <actionType>emailSimple</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailAddresses</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AAkPay__Contact__r.Email</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailSubject</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Your card is expiring soon - keep your BirdLife Australia support going</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>emailBody</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>CardExpiryEmailBody</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>sendRichBody</name>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>emailSimple</nameSegment>
        <versionSegment>1</versionSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>61.0</apiVersion>
    <decisions>
        <name>Can_Email_Donor</name>
        <label>Can we email the donor?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>311</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Expiry_Task_No_Email</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No email possible - task only</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Email_OK</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.AAkPay__Contact__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.AAkPay__Contact__r.Email</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.AAkPay__Contact__r.npsp__Deceased__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.AAkPay__Contact__r.HasOptedOutOfEmail</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Send_Card_Expiry_Email</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Email OK</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Phase 2 of Regular Giving Recovery. Payments2Us automatically sets AAkPay__Expiry_Reminder__c to true when a stored card is within ~31 days of expiry; nothing in the org consumed that flag. This flow fires on that transition for Active recurring payments and emails the donor a self-service card-update link before the payment ever fails (task-only fallback when the donor cannot be emailed). Fires once per flag transition. Built 20 Aug 2026 as Draft - see docs/fundraising/02-automation-regular-giving-recovery.md for the activation gate.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>DueIn7Days</name>
        <dataType>Date</dataType>
        <expression>{!$Flow.CurrentDate} + 7</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>RP aCU - Card Expiry Reminder {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>RP aCU - Card Expiry Reminder</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Expiry_Task_No_Email</name>
        <label>Create expiry task (no email possible)</label>
        <locationX>440</locationX>
        <locationY>431</locationY>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>ActivityDate</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>DueIn7Days</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Description</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>NoEmailExpiryTaskDescription</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>OwnerId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.OwnerId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Priority</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Normal</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Not Started</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Subject</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Card expiring soon on active recurring payment - no email on file - contact donor</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>WhatId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Task</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Can_Email_Donor</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>AAkPay__Expiry_Reminder__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>AAkPay__Recurring_Payment_Status__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Active</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>AAkPay__Recurring_Payment__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Draft</status>
    <textTemplates>
        <name>CardExpiryEmailBody</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>Dear {!$Record.AAkPay__Contact__r.FirstName},

Thank you for your ongoing support of BirdLife Australia.

The card you use for your recurring payment of ${!$Record.AAkPay__Payment_Amount__c} ({!$Record.AAkPay__Frequency__c}) is due to expire soon. To make sure your support continues without interruption, you can update your card details securely here - it only takes a couple of minutes:

https://{!$Record.AAkPay__Email_Card_Update__c}

If your card has already been replaced with the same number and a new expiry date, it may continue to work automatically - but updating your details now is the safest way to avoid a missed payment.

If you have any questions, or would like to change your giving in any way, just reply to this email or give us a call.

Thank you for helping protect Australia's birds.

Warm regards,
BirdLife Australia Supporter Services</text>
    </textTemplates>
    <textTemplates>
        <name>NoEmailExpiryTaskDescription</name>
        <isViewedAsPlainText>true</isViewedAsPlainText>
        <text>The card on this ACTIVE recurring payment is due to expire within ~31 days (Payments2Us expiry reminder flag), and the donor could not be emailed automatically (no contact/email on file, deceased, or email opt-out).

Recurring payment: {!$Record.Name} ({!$Record.AAkPay__Recurring_Payment_No__c})
Amount: ${!$Record.AAkPay__Payment_Amount__c} {!$Record.AAkPay__Frequency__c}
Card expiry: {!$Record.AAkPay__Card_Expiry_Date__c}

Next step: contact the donor by phone or mail to update card details before the payment fails. A new card can be taken via the Card Update action on the Recurring Payment record.</text>
    </textTemplates>
</Flow>
